the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for *a case*.
    the answer to Haftung nach § 823 bgb for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Haftung nach § 823 bgb would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_11_source_references includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/source-references.ruml".

bgh 2024 is published at "https://www.bundesgerichtshof.de/2024/123".

mueller 2024 is published at "https://www.jurpc.de/2024/123".

bmf income tax is published at "https://www.bundesfinanzministerium.de/bmf-schreiben/2024-01-01-einkommensteuer".

Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for a case if
    the answer to Haftung nach § 823 bgb for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Haftung nach § 823 bgb for the case is a truth value
    and Haftung nach § 823 bgb would hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "source-references.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

scenario generated_2 is, as stated in "source-references.ruml" at generated_2:
    % every leaf answered yes
    the answer to Haftung nach § 823 bgb for case 1 is true.
    node_1 expects answers ["Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].

scenario generated_3 is, as stated in "source-references.ruml" at generated_3:
    % the leaf 1 answered no, the others yes
    the answer to Haftung nach § 823 bgb for case 1 is false.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for case 1"].

scenario generated_4 is, as stated in "source-references.ruml" at generated_4:
    % every leaf answered no
    the answer to Haftung nach § 823 bgb for case 1 is false.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for case 1"].

query node_1 is:
    Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Haftung nach § 823 bgb holds for case 1.

